1: # The second boundary of the marked E7 source curve
2: 
3: We retain the actual marked source of SM.7 and the chord-normalized
4: linearization of the K39 working calculation. The following are exact
5: maps on a punctured parameter disc. They do not assign the completed
6: threefold return.
7: 
8: Put v=zeta^(-2). The holomorphic coordinate isomorphism on each nonzero
9: parameter fibre is
10: \[
11:  X=\zeta^{-2}X_\infty,\qquad
12:  Y=\zeta^{-3}Y_\infty,\qquad
13:  T=\zeta^{-4}T_\infty.
14: \]
15: It sends the source equation and marked section to
16: \[
17:  Y_\infty^2=X_\infty^3+(\zeta^2-2)X_\infty^2
18:               +T_\infty X_\infty+\zeta^2,
19:  \qquad G_\infty=(0,\zeta).
20: \]
21: All coefficients extend across zeta=0. The selected value becomes
22: \(T_{\infty,0}=1-2\zeta^2\), and its cubic factors literally as
23: \[
24:  (X_\infty-1)^2(X_\infty+\zeta^2).
25: \]
26: Its normalization is
27: \[
28:  X_\infty=s^2-\zeta^2,\qquad
29:  Y_\infty=s(s^2-\zeta^2-1).
30: \]
31: The double preimages are \(s=\pm\sqrt{1+\zeta^2}\). They remain
32: disjoint across the central parameter. The normalization map is an
33: immersion there: its s derivative has first component 2s, and at s=0
34: its second component is \(-(1+\zeta^2)\), a unit. The zero section
35: gives its smooth infinity point. Thus this selected normalization
36: surface is the literal product \(\mathbf P^1\times D_\zeta\).
37: 
38: At zeta=0 the source cubic discriminant is
39: \(4T_\infty^2(1-T_\infty)\). The unselected double discriminant
40: value is at T_inf=0 and the selected simple value remains T_inf=1.
41: The local simultaneous source resolution at the former is the same
42: rank-one matrix construction as in K39, through the exact coordinates
43: \[
44:  A=Y_\infty-\zeta,\quad B=Y_\infty+\zeta,\quad C=X_\infty,
45:  \quad D=T_\infty+X_\infty^2+(\zeta^2-2)X_\infty,
46:  \qquad AB=CD.
47: \]
48: The marked small resolution is A=Dz, C=Bz. Its projection to zeta is
49: the submersion \(\zeta=(B-Dz)/2\). The selected node lies in the
50: complementary chart, at A=-zeta, C=1, w=zeta, and hence misses this
51: exceptional curve.
52: 
53: The actual Hom factors are also retained. Define
54: \[
55:  F_{21,\infty}
56:   =\frac{Y_\infty+\zeta+(T_\infty/(2\zeta))X_\infty}{X_\infty},
57:  \qquad
58:  F_{12,\infty}
59:   =\frac{Y_\infty-\zeta-(T_\infty/(2\zeta))X_\infty}{X_\infty}.
60: \]
61: The previous factors obey \(F_{ab}=\zeta^{-1}F_{ab,\infty}\).
62: Since \(q=\zeta^{-4}q_\infty\), the actual linearization becomes
63: \[
64:  \phi_{ab}=\frac{q}{vF_{ab}}
65:        =\frac{\zeta^{-1}q_\infty}{F_{ab,\infty}}.
66: \]
67: At the selected node its factors are respectively
68: \(1/(2\zeta)\) and \(-1/(2\zeta)\). Hence
69: \(\phi_{21}/q_\infty=2\) and
70: \(\phi_{12}/q_\infty=-2\), with zero parameter winding. The leading
71: selected Tate coefficient is
72: \[
73:  \frac{q_T}{q_\infty}
74:    =-\frac1{64(1+\zeta^2)^3}+O(q_\infty).
75: \]
76: It is a nonvanishing unit on the parameter disc. The III-star Hom
77: limits are likewise 2 and -2, obtained directly from the displayed
78: T_inf-leading terms. These comparisons retain the original scalar.
79: 
80: The remaining morphism is the actual periodic suspension through the
81: unselected I2 component flop. An extending selected normalization and
82: its units do not supply that exterior suspension map. Its fixed data,
83: marked line and finite-cap boundaries remain part of this calculation.
84: 
85: The common suspension formula also has an exact comparison on the
86: punctured parameter disc. Identify the pullback of each actual source
87: Cartier line with its infinity-chart line by sending the canonical
88: meromorphic divisor section to the same section. Translation by the
89: marked G commutes with the displayed source coordinate isomorphism.
90: Since the primitive lift U_a has target multiplier X(p-G)^{-a}, this
91: line comparison gives
92: \[
93:  I_\zeta U_{a,\mathrm{old}}I_\zeta^{-1}
94:        =\zeta^{2a}U_{a,\infty}.
95: \]
96: The actual degree-two Cartier multiplier satisfies
97: r_old=\zeta^{-2}r_inf; its equal source and target factors cancel
98: when conjugating B. Hence the identity ab=2 gives the literal map
99: \[
100:  I_\zeta B_{a,b,\mathrm{old}}I_\zeta^{-1}
101:  =2(-1)^{b+1}\lambda q_\infty U_{a,\infty}^{,b}.
102: \]
103: The exponent is 2ab-4=0, so this comparison retains the original
104: scalar. Near the unselected I2 point q_inf is a unit with value -1.
105: The finite-cap root maps remain required: the source base coordinate
106: changes by T_old=\zeta^{-4}T_inf, so a root coordinate of order m
107: has the actual comparison z_old^m=\zeta^4 z_inf^m. The displayed
108: source-line map alone does not choose or close this root comparison.
109: 
110: The program code/part3_root/source_infinity_chart.py checks all the
111: displayed substitutions and leading coefficients exactly; its output
112: does not encode a sphere-return value.
113: 
114: The initial program compared factored symbolic expressions structurally;
115: its equivalent opposite-factor forms failed that check. The preserved
116: attempt is under code/part3_root/attempts/source_infinity_structural_comparison.
117: The corrected assertion checks their expanded polynomial difference.
